    {
     "name": "Life story",
     "page": 2,
     "left": 606,
     "top": 212,
     "width": 380,
     "height": 410,
     "size": 13.5,
     "font": "R",
     "color": "#4a4540",
     "multiline": true,
     "align": 0,
     "value": "Eleanor was born on a spring morning in 1941 and spent her childhood on her family’s farm outside Fairview, where she learned to love early sunrises and tomato vines. She taught second grade for thirty-four years and could still name nearly every student she ever had.\n\nShe married her sweetheart, Robert, in 1963, and together they raised three children in a house that was never quiet and always smelled of coffee. Eleanor tended a garden the whole street admired, never missed a grandchild’s recital, and believed that a handwritten letter could fix almost anything.\n\nShe is survived by her children Anna, James and Thomas, seven grandchildren, and countless friends who were made to feel like family the moment they arrived.",
     "lead": 1.65
    }
